# Q15 — PUT environment visible to session shell, isolated from others?
Date: 2026-10-13. Container agency-spike-q. No model needed: direct route
POST /api/session/{id}/shell executes in the session; it shares Shell.Service
with the model shell tool (tool/plugin/shell.ts imports Shell from
../../shell.js), which reads SessionEnvironment.Service (shell.ts:129).

## Commands + trimmed output

$ PUT /api/session/S2/environment {"variables":{"SPIKE_Q15_VAR":"q15-value-1"}}
PUT=204                                        # shape {"variables":{...}}; bare object 400s
$ POST /api/session/S2/shell {"command":"echo VAR-was:${SPIKE_Q15_VAR:-UNSET}"}
SHELL=204
$ GET /api/session/S2/message (shell message, trimmed)
"command":"echo VAR-was:${SPIKE_Q15_VAR:-UNSET}","status":"exited","exit":0,
"output":{"output":"VAR-was:q15-value-1\n",...}   # POSITIVE: sees the variable
$ POST /api/session/S3/shell (same command, no PUT ever) -> 204
$ GET /api/session/S3/message (trimmed)
"output":{"output":"VAR-was:UNSET\n",...}          # NEGATIVE: isolated

## Observation
Yes. One PUT replaces the session's process environment; that session's
shell sees it, a second session does not. Same service feeds model tool
calls, so the envelope/env-file fallback is unnecessary.

## Verdict: yes (no fallback)
